 saved by Dustin Wolf","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:02"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"4"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5080157","displayName":"Frank Nazar","shortName":"F. Nazar"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4587952","displayName":"Dustin Wolf","shortName":"D. Wolf"},"type":"saver"}]},{"id":"401892755000000060","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Icing","type":{"id":"516","text":"Stoppage","abbreviation":"stoppage"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:14"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"}}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1843","fullName":"Scotiabank Saddledome","address":{"city":"Calgary","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1843.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":18411,"officials":[{"fullName":"Mark Shewchyk","displayName":"Mark Shewchyk","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"TJ Luxmore","displayName":"TJ Luxmore","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Michael Markovic","displayName":"Michael Markovic","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Caleb Apperson","displayName":"Caleb Apperson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Sam Rinzel scores in overtime to lift Blackhawks over Flames 4-3","description":"— Sam Rinzel scored in overtime and had two assists to lead the Chicago Blackhawks past the Calgary Flames 4-3 on Saturday, snapping a nine-game road winless skid.","story":"CALGARY, Alberta -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080173/sam-rinzel\">Sam Rinzel</a> scored in overtime and had two assists to lead the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-blackhawks\">Chicago Blackhawks</a> past the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cgy/calgary-flames\">Calgary Flames</a> 4-3 on Saturday, snapping a nine-game road winless skid.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3735/patrick-kane\">Patrick Kane</a> had a goal and two assists for Chicago (7-14-2). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149231/roman-kantserov\">Roman Kantserov</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3115033/ryan-donato\">Ryan Donato</a> also scored. The Blackhawks are 3-1-1 in their last five.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2562636/ryan-strome\">Ryan Strome</a>, who also had an assist, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188608/jonathan-castagna\">Jonathan Castagna</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587843/yegor-sharangovich\">Yegor Sharangovich</a> scored for Calgary (10-12-2).\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565234/spencer-knight\">Spencer Knight</a> had 32 saves for Chicago. He improved to 7-11-1.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587952/dustin-wolf\">Dustin Wolf</a> made 29 stops for the Flames. He fell to 5-6-2.\n\n\r\n              Kane’s three points gives the 38-year-old winger 1,415 for his career (510 goals, 905 assists), moving past Doug Gilmour into 22nd on the NHL’s all-time points list. Adam Oates is 21st at 1,420.\n\n\r\n              Rookie center <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291935/anton-frondell\">Anton Frondell</a> left the game after two periods with an undisclosed injury. Kantserov has 10 goals to lead all rookies. Chicago went 1 for 2 on the power play to improve to 7 for 14 over the last five games.\n\n\r\n              Center <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392883/martin-pospisil\">Martin Pospisil</a> (upper body) left the game late in the second and did not return after he was elbowed in the head by Blackhawks defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697717/wyatt-kaiser\">Wyatt Kaiser</a>, who was assessed a major penalty and game misconduct. Castagna’s first three NHL goals have come in the last three games.\n\n\r\n              On the ensuing power play after Kaiser’s major penalty, Sharangovich one-timed a Strome pass into the top corner at 1:16 of the third period, tying the score 3-3. Allowing the Flames to pick up a point.\n\n\r\n              With two assists, Rinzel is the first defenseman in Blackhawks history to record multiple assists in five consecutive games. The 22-year-old has 11 assists over that span.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blackhawks: At Vancouver on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              Flames: At Ottawa on Monday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-21T23:54:33Z"}}